    "title": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Astro peer conflict**",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Astro peer conflict**\n\nBumping TypeScript to `^6.0.0` leaves `@astrojs/check@0.9.8` on a peer range of `typescript: ^5.0.0`, which makes npm-based installs fail with `ERESOLVE` when resolving `typescript@6.0.3`. This affects documented `npm install` flows and the Docker auto-install fallback path when Bun is unavailable, and leaves the `astro check` toolchain on an unsupported TypeScript version. Updating `@astrojs/check` to a version that supports TypeScript 6, or keeping TypeScript on v5, keeps npm installs usable.\n\n<details><summary><strong>Artifacts</strong></summary><br />\n\n**[Repro: isolated package.json fixture copied from the PR workspace](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/de5121ae-9cd4-4191-a0ab-1858aa3b159d)**\n\n- Contains supporting evidence from the run (application/json; charset=utf-8).\n\n**[Repro: verbose npm install output showing ERESOLVE peer dependency conflict](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/42a3847d-5634-45af-b433-d295495fb26d)**\n\n- Keeps the command output available without making the summary code-heavy.\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/trex/runs/11724789/artifacts?artifact=de5121ae-9cd4-4191-a0ab-1858aa3b159d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifactsDark.svg?v=1\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifacts.svg?v=1\"><img alt=\"View artifacts\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifacts.svg?v=1\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n</details>\n\n<sub><a href=\"https://www.greptile.com/trex\"><img alt=\"T-Rex\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/trex/trex_green.svg\" height=\"14\" align=\"absmiddle\"></a> Ran code and verified through T-Rex</sub>\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/cursor?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20package.json%0ALine%3A%2028%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Astro%20peer%20conflict**%0A%0ABumping%20TypeScript%20to%20%60%5E6.0.0%60%20leaves%20%60%40astrojs%2Fcheck%400.9.8%60%20on%20a%20peer%20range%20of%20%60typescript%3A%20%5E5.0.0%60%2C%20which%20makes%20npm-based%20installs%20fail%20with%20%60ERESOLVE%60%20when%20resolving%20%60typescript%406.0.3%60.%20This%20affects%20documented%20%60npm%20install%60%20flows%20and%20the%20Docker%20auto-install%20fallback%20path%20when%20Bun%20is%20unavailable%2C%20and%20leaves%20the%20%60astro%20check%60%20toolchain%20on%20an%20unsupported%20TypeScript%20version.%20Updating%20%60%40astrojs%2Fcheck%60%20to%20a%20version%20that%20supports%20TypeScript%206%2C%20or%20keeping%20TypeScript%20on%20v5%2C%20keeps%20npm%20installs%20usable.%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&pr=916&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursorDark.svg?v=3\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=3\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=3\" height=\"20\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20package.json%0ALine%3A%2028%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Astro%20peer%20conflict**%0A%0ABumping%20TypeScript%20to%20%60%5E6.0.0%60%20leaves%20%60%40astrojs%2Fcheck%400.9.8%60%20on%20a%20peer%20range%20of%20%60typescript%3A%20%5E5.0.0%60%2C%20which%20makes%20npm-based%20installs%20fail%20with%20%60ERESOLVE%60%20when%20resolving%20%60typescript%406.0.3%60.%20This%20affects%20documented%20%60npm%20install%60%20flows%20and%20the%20Docker%20au