    "title": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **js-yaml override breaks tools**",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **js-yaml override breaks tools**\n\nThe override now forces `js-yaml@5` into dependents that still import `js-yaml` as a default export. With this dependency graph, both `markdownlint-cli2` and Astro fail at startup with `Missing 'default' export in module .../js-yaml.mjs`, so the Docker image verification and local tool runs can stop before linting starts. Keep the override on the v4 line, or update the affected consumers to versions that support the v5 ESM export shape.\n\n<details><summary><strong>Artifacts</strong></summary><br />\n\n**[Repro: generated startup script for markdownlint-cli2 and Astro through the installed dependency graph](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/d177b3ab-ccd2-4fbf-b8b2-540b889e2111)**\n\n- Contains supporting evidence from the run (text/x-shellscript; charset=utf-8).\n\n**[Repro: startup output showing js-yaml 5.0.0 and markdownlint-cli2 missing default export failure](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/508cb034-6587-4753-854c-3239ce05e836)**\n\n- Keeps the command output available without making the summary code-heavy.\n\n**[Repro: bun install output for the PR dependency graph](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/10112bc5-4e39-41ed-a168-6209aecde48e)**\n\n- Keeps the command output available without making the summary code-heavy.\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/trex/runs/11732285/artifacts?artifact=d177b3ab-ccd2-4fbf-b8b2-540b889e2111\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifactsDark.svg?v=1\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifacts.svg?v=1\"><img alt=\"View artifacts\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/ViewArtifacts.svg?v=1\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n</details>\n\n<sub><a href=\"https://www.greptile.com/trex\"><img alt=\"T-Rex\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/trex/trex_green.svg\" height=\"14\" align=\"absmiddle\"></a> Ran code and verified through T-Rex</sub>\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/cursor?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20package.json%0ALine%3A%2034-36%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**js-yaml%20override%20breaks%20tools**%0A%0AThe%20override%20now%20forces%20%60js-yaml%405%60%20into%20dependents%20that%20still%20import%20%60js-yaml%60%20as%20a%20default%20export.%20With%20this%20dependency%20graph%2C%20both%20%60markdownlint-cli2%60%20and%20Astro%20fail%20at%20startup%20with%20%60Missing%20'default'%20export%20in%20module%20...%2Fjs-yaml.mjs%60%2C%20so%20the%20Docker%20image%20verification%20and%20local%20tool%20runs%20can%20stop%20before%20linting%20starts.%20Keep%20the%20override%20on%20the%20v4%20line%2C%20or%20update%20the%20affected%20consumers%20to%20versions%20that%20support%20the%20v5%20ESM%20export%20shape.%0A%0AHow%20can%20I%20resolve%20this%3F%20If%20you%20propose%20a%20fix%2C%20please%20make%20it%20concise.&pr=916&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursorDark.svg?v=3\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=3\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCursor.svg?v=3\" height=\"20\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20package.json%0ALine%3A%2034-36%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**js-yaml%20override%20breaks%20tools**%0A%0AThe%20override%20now%20forces%20%60js-yaml%405%60%20into%20dependents%20that%20still%20import%20%60js-yaml%60%20as%20a%20default%20export.%20With%20this%20dependency%20graph%2C%20both%